---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Wyllex"
  description="How Wyllex handles your early access details and optional website analytics."
>
  <section class="legal-main" data-theme="light">
    <article class="legal-content">
      <div class="eyebrow">THE SMALL PRINT, IN PLAIN ENGLISH.</div>
      <h1>Your privacy.</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Last updated {site.legal.updated}</p>
      <p class="legal-intro">
        Wyllex is an upcoming learning app for Law students. This notice explains how{' '}
        {site.legal.operator} handles personal information on this website and our early access
        waitlist.
      </p>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you join the waitlist, we collect your email address and, if you choose to share it,
        your university. We also save the signup time, the referring website’s domain, and campaign
        labels included in the link you followed. We do not store the full referring URL.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our hosting and service providers may process technical information such as IP addresses and
        request logs to deliver and protect the website.
      </p>
      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your email to confirm your place and send updates about Wyllex early access. Your
        optional university helps us understand where interest comes from. Referral and campaign
        information helps us understand how people find us. We do not sell your information.
      </p>
      <p>
        We rely on your consent for waitlist emails and optional analytics. We rely on our
        legitimate interests in running and securing this website for essential technical
        processing. You can withdraw consent at any time without affecting processing that happened
        before you withdrew it.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics and your choice</h2>
      <p>
        When enabled, we use PostHog only if you choose “Allow analytics”. We record a small set of
        actions: page views, exploring the product demo or a subject, clicking the main call to
        action, and starting or completing signup. We do not send your email, university, form
        contents, or URL query strings to PostHog. We do not enable session recordings, advertising
        trackers, or automatic interaction capture.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use a random identifier kept in page memory to group events during your visit. It resets
        when the page reloads. We ask PostHog not to create person profiles or enrich events with
        location data. Like any network service, its infrastructure receives connection information,
        including your IP address.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your analytics choice is saved in your browser’s local storage so we can remember it. This
        preference is essential to honouring your choice; no optional analytics runs before consent.
        When analytics is configured, you can change your decision using “Privacy choices” in the
        footer. We also respect browser Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals. Blocking
        storage or declining analytics does not prevent you from using the website.
      </p>
      <h2>Who helps us run Wyllex</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare hosts and protects the site. Supabase stores the waitlist. If confirmation emails
        are enabled, Resend delivers them. PostHog processes optional analytics. These providers
        process data to supply their services. Depending on our provider settings and their
        infrastructure, information may be processed outside your country, including in the European
        Economic Area or United States. Where required, we use provider agreements and appropriate
        transfer safeguards.
      </p>
      <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>
        We keep waitlist details until you ask to leave, or for up to 12 months after the app’s
        public launch. If we discontinue the waitlist, we will delete its records within 90 days.
        Analytics retention follows our PostHog project settings. Copies in provider backups may
        remain until their normal backup retention periods expire.
      </p>
      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to access, correct, or delete your details, withdraw consent, or raise a concern
        by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. To leave the
        waitlist, send “Unsubscribe” in the subject line from the address you used to join. We may
        need to verify your identity before acting on a request.
      </p>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may also have rights to restrict or object to processing
        and receive a portable copy of your data. You can complain to your local data protection
        authority. In the UK, this is the{' '}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Information Commissioner’s Office
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>Students under 16</h2>
      <p>
        This waitlist is intended for university students aged 16 or over. If you believe someone
        under 16 has shared personal information with us, contact us so we can remove it.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this notice as Wyllex develops. The date above shows the latest version. For
        privacy questions, contact {site.legal.operator} at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
